A/README.md:22:   applyPatch({}, [{ op: 'remove', path: '/x' }]);
A/README.md:23: } catch (err) {
A/README.md:24:   err instanceof PatchError; // true
A/README.md:25:   err.message; // 'operation 0: path not found'
A/README.md:26:   err.index; // 0
A/README.md:27: }
A/README.md:28: ```
A/README.md:29: 
A/README.md:30: - `parsePointer(pointer)` returns the decoded reference tokens. It throws a `TypeError`
A/README.md:31:   (`pointer must be a string`) for a non-string and a `SyntaxError` (`invalid pointer`) for a
A/README.md:32:   malformed pointer.
A/README.md:33: - `applyPatch(doc, patch)` returns a new document and never changes `doc` or `patch`. The result
A/README.md:34:   shares no object or array with either, keeps member order and keeps `-0`.
A/README.md:35: - Every failure is a `PatchError` with an `index`: `null` with the message
A/README.md:36:   `patch must be an array`, otherwise the index of the failing operation and the message
A/README.md:37:   `operation <i>: <reason>`.
A/README.md:38: 
A/README.md:39: Reasons found while checking the form of each operation (all operations are checked before any
A/README.md:40: is applied): `not an object`, `bad op`, `bad path`, `bad from`, `missing value`,
A/README.md:41: `cannot remove root`, `cannot move into own child`.
A/README.md:42: 
A/README.md:43: Reasons found while applying: `path not found`, `from not found`, `bad index`, `test failed`.
A/README.md:44: 
A/README.md:45: ## Command line
A/README.md:46: 
A/README.md:47: ```sh
A/README.md:48: node jsonpatch-cli.mjs <patch> [<doc>]
A/README.md:49: ```
A/README.md:50: 
A/README.md:51: Reads the patch from the file `<patch>` and the document from the file `<doc>`. A missing
A/README.md:52: `<doc>`, or an argument of `-`, means standard input (only one input may be standard input).
A/README.md:53: Inputs are UTF-8 (a leading byte order mark is ignored), at most 1 MiB, and at most 1000 levels
A/README.md:54: deep. The result is printed as `JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)` followed by a newline.
A/README.md:55: 
A/README.md:56: ```sh
A/README.md:57: echo '{"a":1}' | node jsonpatch-cli.mjs patch.json
A/README.md:58: node jsonpatch-cli.mjs patch.json doc.json > result.json
A/README.md:59: ```
A/README.md:60: 
A/README.md:61: | Exit | Meaning | stderr |
A/README.md:62: | ---- | ------- | ------ |
A/README.md:63: | 0 | success | nothing |
A/README.md:64: | 1 | read error | `Error: <name>: no such file` / `is a directory` / `too large` / `cannot read` |
A/README.md:65: | 2 | wrong arguments | `Usage: node jsonpatch-cli.mjs <patch> [<doc>]` |
A/README.md:66: | 3 | bad input | `Error: <name>: invalid UTF-8` / `invalid JSON` / `too deep` |
A/README.md:67: | 4 | patch failed | `Error: <PatchError message>` |
A/README.md:68: 
A/README.md:69: `<name>` is the argument as given, or `stdin`. The patch input is fully read and checked before
A/README.md:70: the document input is read.
A/README.md:71: 
